  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "This bug is visible in my world at https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_3f6d7439-1d54-4190-b7c5-f96168cd8913 - the glyphs on the wall directly in front of where the player spawns (press the yellow gear) do not render properly in beta 1342.\n\nIn the release build, these all render properly, however in the beta they flicker and swap to the wrong glyph.\n\nThis shader operates by having a texture which is a long strip containing every glyph. The shader does some math to the world position of the mesh (using a random() function that abuses float inaccuracy), and uses that result to select an index, which then becomes an offset in the texture.\n\nGlyphs only disappear because the texture is set to clip rather than repeat, if it were set otherwise it would only appear to choose the wrong glyph.",
